==Old English==
===Etymology===
From [[hlaf|hlāf]] + a second element representing a Germanic ''*deigjōn'' ‘kneader’ (compare Old English[[dǣġe]]).

===Pronunciation===
[[IPA]]: /'hlæ:vdi:je/

===Noun===
'''hlǣfdīġe''' ''f'' (''pl'' '''hlǣfdīgan''')
# a [[lady]], the mistress of a household.

